---@field Runtime aws.mediatailor.RuntimeType|string The expression language used to evaluate expressions in the function configuration. Set this to JSONata.
---@field Output? aws.mediatailor.__mapOf__string A map of output bindings. Each key is a namespaced output path (such as player_params.device_type or temp.variant), and each value is an expression that MediaTailor evaluates at runtime against the current session state. For more information about expression syntax, see JSONata expression reference in the MediaTailor User Guide.

---The configuration for DASH content.
---@class aws.mediatailor.DashConfiguration
---@field ManifestEndpointPrefix? aws.mediatailor.__string The URL that MediaTailor generates to initiate a playback session. The session uses server-side reporting.
---@field DualStackManifestEndpointPrefix? aws.mediatailor.__string The dual-stack (IPv4 and IPv6) URL that MediaTailor generates to initiate a playback session. The session uses server-side reporting.
---@field MpdLocation? aws.mediatailor.__string The setting that controls whether MediaTailor includes the Location tag in DASH manifests. MediaTailor populates the Location tag with the URL for manifest update requests, to be used by players that don't support sticky redirects. Disable this if you have CDN routing rules set up for accessing MediaTailor manifests, and you are either using client-side reporting or your players support sticky HTT...
---@field OriginManifestType? aws.mediatailor.OriginManifestType The setting that controls whether MediaTailor handles manifests from the origin server as multi-period manifests or single-period manifests. If your origin server produces single-period manifests, set this to SINGLE_PERIOD. The default setting is MULTI_PERIOD. For multi-period manifests, omit this setting or set it to MULTI_PERIOD.

---The configuration for DASH PUT operations.
---@class aws.mediatailor.DashConfigurationForPut
---@field MpdLocation? aws.mediatailor.__string The setting that controls whether MediaTailor includes the Location tag in DASH manifests. MediaTailor populates the Location tag with the URL for manifest update requests, to be used by players that don't support sticky redirects. Disable this if you have CDN routing rules set up for accessing MediaTailor manifests, and you are either using client-side reporting or your players support sticky HTT...
---@field OriginManifestType? aws.mediatailor.OriginManifestType|string The setting that controls whether MediaTailor handles manifests from the origin server as multi-period manifests or single-period manifests. If your origin server produces single-period manifests, set this to SINGLE_PERIOD. The default setting is MULTI_PERIOD. For multi-period manifests, omit this setting or set it to MULTI_PERIOD.

