---@field PlaybackEndpointPrefix? aws.mediatailor.__string The playback endpoint prefix associated with the playback configuration.
---@field DualStackPlaybackEndpointPrefix? aws.mediatailor.__string The dual-stack (IPv4 and IPv6) playback endpoint prefix associated with the playback configuration.
---@field SessionInitializationEndpointPrefix? aws.mediatailor.__string The session initialization endpoint prefix associated with the playback configuration.
---@field DualStackSessionInitializationEndpointPrefix? aws.mediatailor.__string The dual-stack (IPv4 and IPv6) session initialization endpoint prefix associated with the playback configuration.
---@field SlateAdUrl? aws.mediatailor.__string The URL for a high-quality video asset to transcode and use to fill in time that's not used by ads. AWS Elemental MediaTailor shows the slate to fill in gaps in media content. Configuring the slate is optional for non-VPAID configurations. For VPAID, the slate is required because MediaTailor provides it in the slots that are designated for dynamic ad content. The slate must be a high-quality asset...
---@field Tags? aws.mediatailor.__mapOf__string The tags to assign to the playback configuration. Tags are key-value pairs that you can associate with Amazon resources to help with organization, access control, and cost tracking. For more information, see Tagging AWS Elemental MediaTailor Resources.
---@field TranscodeProfileName? aws.mediatailor.__string The name that is used to associate this playback configuration with a custom transcode profile. This overrides the dynamic transcoding defaults of MediaTailor. Use this only if you have already set up custom profiles with the help of AWS Support.
---@field VideoContentSourceUrl? aws.mediatailor.__string The URL prefix for the parent manifest for the stream, minus the asset ID. The maximum length is 512 characters.
---@field AdConditioningConfiguration? aws.mediatailor.AdConditioningConfiguration The setting that indicates what conditioning MediaTailor will perform on ads that the ad decision server (ADS) returns, and what priority MediaTailor uses when inserting ads.
---@field AdDecisionServerConfiguration? aws.mediatailor.AdDecisionServerConfiguration The configuration for customizing HTTP requests to the ad decision server (ADS). This includes settings for request method, headers, body content, and compression options.
---@field YieldOptimizationConfiguration? aws.mediatailor.YieldOptimizationConfiguration Configuration for Yield Optimization, which fills unsold ad inventory in ad breaks with programmatic ads from Amazon Publisher Services (APS).
---@field FunctionMapping? aws.mediatailor.FunctionMapping A map of lifecycle hook event names to function identifiers. The function mapping specifies which function MediaTailor executes at each lifecycle hook during ad insertion. Valid keys are PRE_SESSION_INITIALIZATION, POST_ORIGIN_RESPONSE, PRE_ADS_REQUEST, POST_ADS_RESPONSE, and PRE_MANIFEST_INSERTION. For more information, see Functions lifecycle hooks in the MediaTailor User Guide.
---@field AdsPersonalizationTimeouts? aws.mediatailor.AdsPersonalizationTimeouts The timeout settings for ad decision server interactions. These settings control how long MediaTailor waits for ADS responses and the total time budget for ad personalization across live, VOD, and prefetch workflows.
---@field AdsPersonalizationConcurrency? aws.mediatailor.AdsPersonalizationConcurrency The concurrency settings for ad decision server interactions. These settings control how many simultaneous ADS requests MediaTailor makes per manifest request.
---@field BeaconingConfiguration? aws.mediatailor.BeaconingConfiguration The beaconing configuration for this playback configuration, which controls whether MediaTailor includes beacons of its own in the ad tracking response.

---The settings that determine how and when MediaTailor places prefetched ads into upcoming ad breaks for recurring prefetch scedules.
---@class aws.mediatailor.RecurringConsumption
---@field RetrievedAdExpirationSeconds? aws.mediatailor.__integer The number of seconds that an ad is available for insertion after it was prefetched.
---@field AvailMatchingCriteria? aws.mediatailor.__listOfAvailMatchingCriteria The configuration for the dynamic variables that determine which ad breaks that MediaTailor inserts prefetched ads in.

---The configuration that defines how MediaTailor performs recurring prefetch.
---@class aws.mediatailor.RecurringPrefetchConfiguration
---@field StartTime? aws.mediatailor.__timestampUnix The start time for the window that MediaTailor prefetches and inserts ads in a live event.
---@field EndTime aws.mediatailor.__timestampUnix The end time for the window that MediaTailor prefetches and inserts ads in a live event.
---@field RecurringConsumption aws.mediatailor.RecurringConsumption The settings that determine how and when MediaTailor places prefetched ads into upcoming ad breaks for recurring prefetch scedules.
---@field RecurringRetrieval aws.mediatailor.RecurringRetrieval The configuration for prefetch ad retrieval from the ADS.

---With recurring prefetch, MediaTailor automatically prefetches ads for every avail that occurs during the retrieval window. The following configurations describe the MediaTailor behavior when prefetching ads for a live event.
---@class aws.mediatailor.RecurringRetrieval
---@field DynamicVariables? aws.mediatailor.__mapOf__string The dynamic variables to use for substitution during prefetch requests to the ADS.
---@field DelayAfterAvailEndSeconds? aws.mediatailor.__integer The number of seconds that MediaTailor waits after an ad avail before prefetching ads for the next avail. If not set, the default is 0 (no delay).
---@field TrafficShapingType? aws.mediatailor.TrafficShapingType|string Indicates the type of traffic shaping used to limit the number of requests to the ADS at one time.
---@field TrafficShapingRetrievalWindow? aws.mediatailor.TrafficShapingRetrievalWindow The configuration that tells Elemental MediaTailor how many seconds to spread out requests to the ad decision server (ADS). Instead of sending ADS requests for all sessions at the same time, MediaTailor spreads the requests across the amount of time specified in the retrieval window.
---@field TrafficShapingTpsConfiguration? aws.mediatailor.TrafficShapingTpsConfiguration The configuration for TPS-based traffic shaping. This approach limits requests to the ad decision server (ADS) based on transactions per second and concurrent users.

