---The segment delivery configuration settings.
---@class aws.mediatailor.SegmentDeliveryConfiguration
---@field BaseUrl? aws.mediatailor.__string The base URL of the host or path of the segment delivery server that you're using to serve segments. This is typically a content delivery network (CDN). The URL can be absolute or relative. To use an absolute URL include the protocol, such as https://example.com/some/path. To use a relative URL specify the relative path, such as /some/path*.
---@field Name? aws.mediatailor.__string A unique identifier used to distinguish between multiple segment delivery configurations in a source location.

---The segmentation_descriptor message can contain advanced metadata fields, like content identifiers, to convey a wide range of information about the ad break. MediaTailor writes the ad metadata in the egress manifest as part of the EXT-X-DATERANGE or EventStream ad marker's SCTE-35 data.
---@class aws.mediatailor.SegmentationDescriptor
---@field SegmentationEventId? number The Event Identifier to assign to the segmentation_descriptor.segmentation_event_id message, as defined in section 10.3.3.1 of the 2022 SCTE-35 specification. The default value is 1.
---@field SegmentationUpidType? number The Upid Type to assign to the segmentation_descriptor.segmentation_upid_type message, as defined in section 10.3.3.1 of the 2022 SCTE-35 specification. Values must be between 0 and 256, inclusive. The default value is 14.
---@field SegmentationUpid? string The Upid to assign to the segmentation_descriptor.segmentation_upid message, as defined in section 10.3.3.1 of the 2022 SCTE-35 specification. The value must be a hexadecimal string containing only the characters 0 though 9 and A through F. The default value is "" (an empty string).
---@field SegmentationTypeId? number The Type Identifier to assign to the segmentation_descriptor.segmentation_type_id message, as defined in section 10.3.3.1 of the 2022 SCTE-35 specification. Values must be between 0 and 256, inclusive. The default value is 48.
---@field SegmentNum? number The segment number to assign to the segmentation_descriptor.segment_num message, as defined in section 10.3.3.1 of the 2022 SCTE-35 specification Values must be between 0 and 256, inclusive. The default value is 0.
---@field SegmentsExpected? number The number of segments expected, which is assigned to the segmentation_descriptor.segments_expectedS message, as defined in section 10.3.3.1 of the 2022 SCTE-35 specification Values must be between 0 and 256, inclusive. The default value is 0.
---@field SubSegmentNum? number The sub-segment number to assign to the segmentation_descriptor.sub_segment_num message, as defined in section 10.3.3.1 of the 2022 SCTE-35 specification. Values must be between 0 and 256, inclusive. The defualt value is null.
---@field SubSegmentsExpected? number The number of sub-segments expected, which is assigned to the segmentation_descriptor.sub_segments_expected message, as defined in section 10.3.3.1 of the 2022 SCTE-35 specification. Values must be between 0 and 256, inclusive. The default value is null.

---@alias aws.mediatailor.SegmentationDescriptorList aws.mediatailor.SegmentationDescriptor[]

---The configuration for a SEQUENTIAL_EXECUTOR function. A SEQUENTIAL_EXECUTOR runs a sequence of child functions in order, passing data between steps through temporary data. For more information, see SEQUENTIAL_EXECUTOR in the MediaTailor User Guide.
---@class aws.mediatailor.SequentialExecutorConfiguration
---@field Runtime aws.mediatailor.RuntimeType|string The expression language used to evaluate expressions in the function configuration. Set this to JSONata.
---@field Output? aws.mediatailor.__mapOf__string An optional map of output bindings that controls which bindings the sequence commits to the session state after all steps complete. If omitted, MediaTailor commits all accumulated output bindings from all child steps.
---@field FunctionList aws.mediatailor.__listOfFunctionsRef An ordered list of 1 to 10 steps. Each step specifies a child function to execute and an optional run condition expression that controls whether the step runs. MediaTailor executes steps in order, passing data between steps through temporary data.
---@field TimeoutMilliseconds aws.mediatailor.__integer The maximum time, in milliseconds, for the entire sequence to complete. This timeout covers all steps, including any HTTP calls made by child functions. If the sequence exceeds this timeout, MediaTailor discards all output from the sequence and proceeds with default behavior.

